      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, the /s/ sound is primarily a stream of turbulent, hissing air with no vibration. To feel the difference, place your fingers lightly on your larynx (Adam's apple) while saying both sounds. When producing /s/, you should feel very little, if any, pulsation. However, when you say /z/, you should distinctly feel your vocal cords vibrating beneath your fingertips.",
